WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:01.390
All right, welcome back.

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:04.100
Uh, I guess to myself, I'm back from Los Angeles.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:07.120
I was on the Joe Rogan experience, one of
the world

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:13.799
biggest podcasts and youtube shows thanks
to Ben Dickson who filled in for me on sort

00:00:13.799 --> 00:00:14.799
of short notice.

00:00:14.799 --> 00:00:17.070
I mean it came, the Joe Rogan thing came together
pretty quickly.

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:23.060
I didn't even know that I was going to be
going to Los Angeles this week until the day

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:29.390
I believe it was that I was leaving on the
end of May break, which had been planned a

00:00:29.390 --> 00:00:30.570
long time in advance.

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:35.220
So thanks to everybody who understands that
this was a big opportunity and I didn't intend

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:36.780
to immediately leave the show again.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.680
So quickly after that, that brief break at
the end of May.

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:45.280
Oh, I also, I guess should thank all the trolls
for those nice messages leading up to the

00:00:45.280 --> 00:00:46.280
interview.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:47.280
David, you're going to bomb.

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:51.310
I can't wait to see Joe Rogan wipe the floor
with you.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:53.780
You're going to embarrass yourself and all
of that stuff.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.809
And the funny thing sort of is that when someone
sends a message like that, I actually wonder

00:00:58.809 --> 00:01:05.510
if that person has never seen Rogan's show
or maybe has never seen my show because Rogan

00:01:05.510 --> 00:01:12.780
has long form conversations with people, uh,
and owning or whatever is not really his thing.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:16.880
I mean sometimes people do end up getting
exposed on his show as we pointed out, like

00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.729
when Candice Owens or Dave Rubin go on there
or a Ben Shapiro goes on and says things that

00:01:21.729 --> 00:01:22.830
don't make any sense.

00:01:22.830 --> 00:01:26.330
But in any case I think it went really well
overall.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:32.030
Um, I'm very self critical and in watching
it back after the fact, I don't think I handled

00:01:32.030 --> 00:01:37.060
every aspect of the two plus hour conversation
as well as I would have wanted or maybe would

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:40.659
have if I had known in advance exactly what
the topics would be.

00:01:40.659 --> 00:01:41.659
But that's the whole thing.

00:01:41.659 --> 00:01:45.900
It's sort of an unplanned, informal, a long
form conversation.

00:01:45.900 --> 00:01:48.200
And I know that I'm a huge self critic.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:53.159
Many areas for improvement would have liked
to have been more clear in some areas, but

00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:55.770
it was really a great opportunity for the
show.

00:01:55.770 --> 00:01:57.659
It's already had a nice impact on the show.

00:01:57.659 --> 00:02:04.460
Nice boost on Youtube, nice boost on podcast
subscribers, modest paid membership boost.

00:02:04.460 --> 00:02:10.060
Although the thing about that is it takes
a while to convert a new viewer to a member,

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:14.950
since you don't immediately become a paid
member of a show, as soon as you hear about

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:17.300
it, most people don't anyway.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:21.660
You hear about a show, then you watch it or
listen to it for awhile, and then some portion

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:24.120
of those people later become paid members.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:31.680
So my, my hope is that in the next four to
12 weeks we'll convert a lot of that new audience

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:34.690
into paid subscribers and that'll be a really
great thing.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:41.860
Um, also had a great dinner with destiny and
Sohn piker and my manager who all of whom

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:43.420
are out in Los Angeles.

00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:46.450
There are some pictures on my Instagram from
that.

00:02:46.450 --> 00:02:51.660
Uh, I was on another show while in La called
exploring minds with Michelle Carol, who's

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.819
an actress who also now has an interview show.

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:56.760
And I had about an hour conversation with
her.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:57.970
It hasn't been published yet.

00:02:57.970 --> 00:03:00.769
I think it will be pretty soon.

00:03:00.769 --> 00:03:06.620
And I posted a picture from that behind the
scenes picture of Michelle and, uh, have me

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.970
on the Instagram account.

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:08.970
So check it out.

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.190
Overall, huge, huge win in the battle of ideas.

00:03:13.190 --> 00:03:19.400
There were moments on the Rogan show where
Joe and I disagreed and I think those were

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:22.769
some of the best moments and it was fine and
it was not awkward and it was as respectful

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:24.319
as I imagined that it would be.

00:03:24.319 --> 00:03:31.220
A, we talked about what constitutes a homophobic
slur in the context of Youtube's terms of

00:03:31.220 --> 00:03:35.680
service, in terms of conditions, how to figure
out whether a company is liberal or conservative.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.239
And we had disagreements and uh, it was, it
was absolutely great to have them and I hope

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:43.920
that it was productive in a sense for the
audience.

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:49.700
So, hi to everyone who has learned about this
show over the last three days.

00:03:49.700 --> 00:03:54.959
Sorry, I guess to everybody who was waiting
for my appearance on Joe Rogan to go so poorly,

00:03:54.959 --> 00:04:00.030
to be such an embarrassment to us, just such
a shameful face plant that it would decimate

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.590
the David Pakman show.

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:04.930
Um, I apologize if that's what you were expecting.

00:04:04.930 --> 00:04:09.879
Onward and upward to more things and expansion
and more announcements coming soon.

00:04:09.879 --> 00:04:18.079
Um, I did unfortunately have to mute hundreds
of people on Twitter after these appearances

00:04:18.079 --> 00:04:22.529
because of the amount of just vitriolic trolling.

00:04:22.529 --> 00:04:27.490
But my new approaches, I don't even think
about engaging with the nonsense on Twitter

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:28.849
or social media.

00:04:28.849 --> 00:04:30.969
I see it, I mute it.

00:04:30.969 --> 00:04:33.130
I don't have to think about it again.

00:04:33.130 --> 00:04:38.539
And I strongly, strongly advise other people
in the audience to do the same thing.

00:04:38.539 --> 00:04:42.119
Uh, unfortunately some of the people in the
audience are the ones doing the trolling and

00:04:42.119 --> 00:04:44.090
so they probably won't take that advice.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:49.939
But if you're a good faith actor on social
media, I'm telling you, I am doing much better

00:04:49.939 --> 00:04:55.830
in terms of everything, productivity, focus,
uh, concentrating on the right things over

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:56.830
the noise.

00:04:56.830 --> 00:05:01.520
Uh, since I have just started this policy
of no engagement with trolls, mute them, don't

00:05:01.520 --> 00:05:02.520
think about them again.

00:05:02.520 --> 00:05:03.419
Uh, that's, that's my advice to you.

